"""
The set of dashboard environment variables actually referenced by a single chart, covering both the
env vars the chart *defines* (when the chart is itself a control such as a categorical dropdown,
calendar, or slider) and the env vars the chart *consumes* via `{IDENTIFIER}` interpolation across:

* the chart's pipeline SQL (every `query.sql` on the pipeline)
* the chart's pipeline node DAG — `formula` / `edit_column` (`formula_arg`), `filter` (per-column
  `operand`), and `add_column_case_statement` (`operand` / `value` / `default`)
* the chart's settings `title` and `subtitle`
* for `text` / `link` charts: the body content (`content`, `display_text`, `url`)
* for `rich_text` charts: ADF text nodes and link `href` marks in the body

Identifiers that do not correspond to a dashboard env var (e.g. unbound template placeholders or
built-in tokens like `{TABLE_NAME.RAW}`) are silently dropped.
"""
type AVPChartUsedEnvVars {
  "ID of the chart on the dashboard."
  chartId: ID!
  "IDs of the dashboard env vars referenced by the chart, sorted by env var name."
  envVarIds: [ID!]!
}

