"""
Whether the organisation's boundaryEnforced setting can be changed right now, and if not, what is
blocking the change. Editability is a property of the organisation's live Units lifecycle rather
than of its configuration - an in-flight Unit merge or transfer, or a change still inside its
cooldown window, locks the setting - so unlike the rest of AdminOrgUnitsSettings this is a
point-in-time answer read from collaboration-context-manager, and it must not be cached alongside
the stable Units configuration. It deliberately does not repeat the value of the setting: read
boundaryEnforced on the parent for that.
"""
type AdminUnitsBoundaryEnforcedEditability {
  """
  What is blocking the change, empty when editable is true. Blocker values that this schema does
  not know about are omitted, so an empty list does not imply editability: use editable for that.
  """
  blockers: [AdminBoundaryEnforcedBlocker!]
  """
  The absolute instant at which the cooldown window expires. Only set when blockers contains
  COOLDOWN_ACTIVE, null otherwise.
  """
  cooldownExpiresAt: DateTime
  """
  True if and only if the setting can be changed. Passed through from
  collaboration-context-manager rather than derived from blockers, so it stays correct even when
  upstream reports a blocker this schema does not yet know about. This describes the state of the
  organisation, not the caller's permission: an editable of true does not mean the calling user is
  allowed to toggle the setting.
  """
  editable: Boolean
}

