"""
A single field an admin must fill in to configure a custom auth connection.

Deliberately kept field-for-field identical in shape to McpAdminManagementMcpServerExtraInput so a
client can render both with one component. `target` is the single intentional difference: an MCP
extra input always feeds a server URL placeholder, whereas a custom auth field may feed the
client ID, the client secret, or a template value.
